!**/.env.example
!apps/*/.env.prod
!.env.sample
# TASK-583: .env.test is generated by `pnpm setup:test` from .env.sample and
# is no longer tracked (matches .env.dev's existing gitignored/generated
# model) — CI never reads this file (CI=true skips file-loading entirely in
# both the TS and Python loaders), so untracking it has no CI impact and
# closes the repeated real-Vault-secret-in-a-tracked-file incident TASK-582
# found. See docs/architecture/environment-configuration-reference.md.
# TASK-584: production reference templates (formerly `.env.production`) were
# relocated per-service and renamed `.env.prod` — the `!apps/*/.env.prod`
# allowlist only un-ignores those; a hypothetical root-level `.env.prod`
# stays ignored, since production references no longer live at the monorepo
# root at all.
# TASK-585: the root `.env.example` (bootstrap floor) was folded into
# `.env.sample` as its first generated section — there is no longer a
# standalone root `.env.example` file, so the root-specific `!.env.example`
# allowlist entry was dropped. `!**/.env.example` stays: it un-ignores the
# unrelated `.example`-named fixtures still in use elsewhere (apps/example,
# apps/ui-playground, docs/archive/**, docs/research/**, the pgbouncer
# validation fixture).
# keep below
!packages/applications/src/common/env

# Local MCP-server config — holds per-developer secrets (e.g. GitLab OAuth
